    "findings": [
      {
        "id": "F1",
        "title": "No iris / pupil / ciliary body / anterior or posterior chamber in the model source",
        "detail": "The strings 'iris', 'pupil', 'ciliary' and 'chamber' occur 0 times in Good_Eye.blend. The absence is a model design decision, not a mapping omission. Knowledge-base cards for these structures remain valid for the KB even without Unity components."
      },
      {
        "id": "F2",
        "title": "vitreous_body is NOT present in the blend source",
        "detail": "The string 'vitreous' occurs 0 times in Good_Eye.blend, while the mapping docx lists unity_name 'vitreous_body' for comp_vitreous. Either the object was added directly in Unity (newer Unity scene than this blend) or this blend is an older revision. ACTION: verify 'vitreous_body' in the Unity Hierarchy."
      },
      {
        "id": "F3",
        "title": "muscle_2 numbering gap originates in the blend source",
        "detail": "The blend contains muscle_0, muscle_1, muscle_3, muscle_4, muscle_5, muscle_6 (no muscle_2). All six real extraocular muscles are present; the gap is a leftover from a deleted object in the original Blender file, not a Unity import issue."
      },
      {
        "id": "F4",
        "title": "7 model objects had no mapping rows; registered here as model_only",
        "detail": "eye (suspected root/controller) and 6 cornea annotation objects (3 Labels + 3 Leader lines for epithelium/stroma/endothelium) existed in the model but were absent from the mapping docx. They carry no anatomical knowledge component (component_id '—') and are registered for model inventory completeness; relevant if AR labeling features are planned."
      },
      {
        "id": "F5",
        "title": "Four DR lesion objects added to the model source (2026-11-08)",
        "detail": "The model team reported adding Microaneurysms, Haemorrhages, Soft_Exudates and Hard_Exudates as new Blender objects representing diabetic retinopathy signs (DIS-001). Object names above are taken verbatim from the user report and appended to blender_objects_found; they have not yet been re-extracted by the string-audit method. Parent hierarchy confirmed by the model team on 2026-11-08: all four objects are parented under eye_sphere_inside (the retina mesh, comp_retina), matching the anatomical location of the lesions on the retinal surface. Registered as rows 45-48 (comp_lesion_microaneurysms, comp_lesion_hemorrhages, comp_lesion_soft_exudates, comp_lesion_hard_exudates, category=Pathology, reference_category=model_only) and linked to the diabetic_retinopathy card via component_ids and AFFECTS relationships. Terminology note: card sign 'Cotton wool spots' = soft exudates (same lesion, two names); 'Haemorrhages' covers card signs 'Intraretinal hemorrhages' and 'Vitreous or preretinal hemorrhage'."
      }
